{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 jupiter.stigmergy.systems 'cd ~/ci/datomworld-floatkind && nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure/reader.cljc | sed -n \\\"1,360p\\\" && git diff origin/master...HEAD -- src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc src/cljs/datomworld/demo && ls .cpcache/*.cp' \"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yang.clojure.reader\n     2\t  \"Frontend-owned, token-aware Clojure source reader (architect ruling\n     3\t   1795693415000, RULING 2).\n     4\t\n     5\t   Consumes original Clojure source text directly and materializes numeric\n     6\t   tokens through `yang.core.numeric-token/materialize :clojure` AT TOKEN\n     7\t   TIME, before any collection (`{...}`, `#{...}`) or downstream lowering can\n     8\t   erase kind or coalesce distinct numeric kinds (such as `1` vs `1.0`).\n     9\t\n    10\t   Explicit lexical coverage:\n    11\t   - Whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF, FF, comma) and comments (`;`, `#!`)\n    12\t   - Strings (`\\\"...\\\"`) with standard escapes (`\\\\\\\"`, `\\\\\\\\`, `\\\\n`, `\\\\r`,\n    13\t     `\\\\t`, `\\\\b`, `\\\\f`, `\\\\uXXXX`, octal `\\\\NNN`)\n    14\t   - Character literals (`\\\\a`, `\\\\newline`, `\\\\space`, `\\\\tab`, `\\\\backspace`,\n    15\t     `\\\\formfeed`, `\\\\return`, `\\\\uXXXX`, `\\\\oNNN`)\n    16\t   - Numeric tokens (exact integers, hex/octal/Nr radix, N big-int, binary64\n    17\t     floats including integral floats and floats beyond 2^53, decimal M,\n    18\t     ratios) via `yang.core.numeric-token`\n    19\t   - Symbolic values (`##Inf`, `##-Inf`, `##NaN`)\n    20\t   - Keywords (`:k`, `:ns/k`), symbols, booleans (`true`, `false`), `nil`\n    21\t   - Collections: lists `(...)`, vectors `[...]`, maps `{...}` (even count\n    22\t     and duplicate-key checks), sets `#{...}` (duplicate-element check),\n    23\t     namespaced maps `#:ns{...}`\n    24\t   - Reader macros: quote `'`, deref `@`, var `#'`, metadata `^:k` / `^Sym` /\n    25\t     `^\\\"s\\\"` / `^{...}`, unquote `~`, unquote-splicing `~@`\n    26\t   - Dispatch forms: `#{...}`, `#_` (with syntax validation of discarded\n    27\t     forms), `#'`, `##`, `#\\\"...\\\"`, `#(...)`, `#:ns{...}`\n    28\t   - Explicit refusals: reader conditionals (`#?`, `#?@`), eval (`#=`),\n    29\t     unknown tagged literals (`#tag`), invalid numeric tokens, malformed\n    30\t     maps/sets/strings/chars, unmatched or unclosed delimiters.\n    31\t\n    32\t   Zero ambient mutable state: no `*data-readers*`, no `*read-eval*`, no\n    33\t   evaluation during reading, no global reader monkeypatching.\"\n    34\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    35\t            [yang.core.numeric-token :as numeric-token]))\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t(defn- reader-error!\n    39\t  ([msg] (reader-error! msg {}))\n    40\t  ([msg data]\n    41\t   (throw (ex-info msg (merge {:type :reader-exception\n    42\t                               :ex-kind :reader-error}\n    43\t                              data)))))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn- char-at\n    47\t  [^String s ^long i]\n    48\t  #?(:cljs (.charAt s i)\n    49\t     :default (.charAt s i)))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn- char-code\n    53\t  [ch]\n    54\t  #?(:cljs (.charCodeAt ch 0)\n    55\t     :default (int ch)))\n    56\t\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn- code->char\n    59\t  [n]\n    60\t  #?(:cljs (js/String.fromCharCode n)\n    61\t     :default (char n)))\n    62\t\n    63\t\n    64\t(defn- whitespace?\n    65\t  [ch]\n    66\t  (let [c (char-code ch)]\n    67\t    (or (= c 32)   ;; space\n    68\t        (= c 9)    ;; \\t\n    69\t        (= c 10)   ;; \\n\n    70\t        (= c 13)   ;; \\r\n    71\t        (= c 12)   ;; \\f\n    72\t        (= c 44)))) ;; comma\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- digit?\n    76\t  [ch]\n    77\t  (let [c (char-code ch)]\n    78\t    (and (<= 48 c) (<= c 57))))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn- hex-digit?\n    82\t